## When to reach for SDD

SDD pays off when the cost of the agent guessing wrong is higher than the cost
of writing the spec.

| Task | Use SDD? |
|---|---|
| New feature touching >3 files | Yes |
| Schema migration / backfill | Yes (always) |
| Refactor with API changes | Yes |
| Pipeline rebuild (dbt, Airflow, …) | Yes |
| New RAG or eval pipeline | Yes |
| Bug fix in 1–2 files | No — go straight to `/plan` |
| Lint / docstring / config tweak | No |
| Spike / prototype | No |

> *"If you'd be annoyed to have the agent interpret requirements differently
> than you meant, write the spec. If you could fix the output in a quick
> follow-up prompt, skip it."*
> — Augment Code, April 2026
