## Spec-Kit (configured)

Spec-Kit is greenfield-first: multi-artifact spec → plan → research → data-model
→ tasks, with a built-in `/speckit-analyze` quality gate. Typical spec volume
~800 lines.

### One-time install

```bash
uv tool install specify-cli --from git+https://github.com/github/spec-kit.git
specify check
```

### Initialise inside this project

> The Copier `_tasks` step already runs this for you when the CLI is on
> `PATH` at generation time. The block below is the manual fallback.

```bash
specify init . --here --integration {{ sdd_install_agent }} --force
```

`--integration` replaced the older `--ai` flag with the plugin-architecture
migration (Spec-Kit ≥ v0.8). Run `specify check` to see all integrations
your installed CLI supports — at time of writing the list includes
`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `cursor`, `copilot` and several more.

### Memory architecture

| File | Contents | Read by |
|---|---|---|
| `.specify/memory/constitution.md` | Architectural principles, non-negotiable | Spec-Kit (every phase) |
| `AGENTS.md` (repo root) | Executor rules, QA commands | All agents |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Claude-Code glue (model + permissions) | Claude Code only |

On conflict, precedence is **Constitution > spec.md > plan.md > tasks.md > code**.

### What gets generated

```
.specify/
├── memory/constitution.md      # architectural principles (non-negotiable)
├── scripts/                    # env validation & helpers
├── specs/<feature>/            # spec.md, plan.md, research.md, data-model.md, tasks.md
└── templates/                  # markdown skeletons
```

### Workflow

```
/speckit-constitution     → write the non-negotiables once per project
/speckit-specify <feat>   → spec.md (what / why, technology-agnostic)
/speckit-clarify          → resolve ambiguities before planning
/speckit-plan             → plan.md (technical architecture, the "how")
/speckit-tasks            → tasks.md (atomic, TDD-ready, [P] = parallel)
/speckit-analyze          → quality gate across all artefacts
/speckit-implement        → execute tasks in order
```

### Update later

```bash
uv tool install specify-cli --force --from git+https://github.com/github/spec-kit.git
```
