## OpenSpec (configured)

OpenSpec is brownfield-first: short delta proposals on a living master spec.
Typical spec volume ~250 lines. Three phases: propose → apply → archive.

### One-time install

Requires Node.js 20.19+.

```bash
npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec@latest
openspec --version
```

### Initialise inside this project

> The Copier `_tasks` step already runs this for you when the CLI is on
> `PATH` at generation time. The block below is the manual fallback.

```bash
openspec init --tools {{ sdd_install_agent }} --force
```

`--tools` accepts a comma-separated list (`claude,cursor`) or `all`. The
upstream [supported-tools list](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec/blob/main/docs/supported-tools.md)
covers 30+ agents (including `claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `cursor`,
`cline`, `windsurf`, `kilocode`, `gemini`, …). Note that OpenSpec uses
`github-copilot`, not `copilot` — if you picked `copilot` in the template
question, re-run init with `--tools github-copilot`.

### Memory architecture

| File | Contents | Read by |
|---|---|---|
| `openspec/AGENTS.md` | Lightweight constitution (project-wide rules) | OpenSpec (every phase) |
| `openspec/project.md` | Stack, conventions | OpenSpec |
| `AGENTS.md` (repo root) | Executor rules, QA commands | All agents |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Claude-Code glue | Claude Code only |

There are **two** `AGENTS.md` files. The repo-root one is generic agent
guardrails; the one in `openspec/` is OpenSpec-specific architecture rules.

### What gets generated

```
openspec/
├── AGENTS.md         # lightweight constitution (project-wide rules)
├── project.md        # stack, conventions
├── specs/            # living master spec (filled by /opsx:archive)
└── changes/          # active change proposals
```

### Workflow

```
/opsx:propose <change>   → openspec/changes/<change>/proposal.md (+ optional design.md)
/opsx:apply              → execute tasks.md
/opsx:archive            → merge delta into openspec/specs/
```

Delta markers (`ADDED`, `MODIFIED`, `REMOVED`) make drift explicit — you see
exactly what changes between the proposal and the current system.

### Brownfield tip

For deeper context acquisition on a legacy codebase, configure
[Repomix MCP](https://github.com/yamadashy/repomix) before running
`/opsx:propose`. It indexes the codebase so the agent can search rather than
guess.

### Update later

```bash
npm update -g @fission-ai/openspec
openspec --version
```
